    \"a-wide\" wins by ID order"
  --- PASS: TestCHK_RegionAndDataNodeAgree (0.02s)
The two strings were extracted from ONE full-page response by regex, HTML-
unescaped and whitespace-normalised, then compared for equality; the test also
requires the region to be non-empty and to name the contested basename, so the
equality is not vacuously true of two empty strings.
(On a partial-swap response only the data node is present — the region lives
outside the #accounts-list swap target by design — so the comparison is
correctly scoped to the full page.)

